# Line endings.
#
# The repository is edited from Windows *and* from the Linux dev
# container, which bind-mounts the same working tree and the same .git.
# One tree cannot hold two conventions, so the endings are pinned here
# instead of being left to each side's core.autocrlf: attributes win
# over autocrlf, so both gits see identical bytes and neither reports
# phantom "whole file changed" diffs.
#
# LF in the index and LF in the working tree, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the exception: CRLF in the working tree on
# every platform (eol=crlf is not platform-dependent, so this still
# looks the same from both sides). Linux never executes them.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touch these, whatever the content sniffing thinks.
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.wad binary
*.lmp binary
*.dat binary
